<title>ZIMBABWE: Zimbabwe's Tanganda yr shr, div fall.</title>
<headline>Zimbabwe's Tanganda yr shr, div fall.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended October 31.</p>
<p>	     (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)			     30.3 vs 39.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			     11.0 making total of 15 vs 20</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    17.9 vs 26.6</p>
<p>    Net interest (paid)/received    (0.9) vs 1.1</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			17.0 vs 27.8</p>
<p>    Taxation				 0.9 vs 6.7</p>
<p>    Attributable profit		 16.1 vs 21.1</p>
<p>    Turnover			     132.8 vs 108.9</p>
<p>Div payable March 10 on register February 28.</p>
<p>Full name: Tanganda Tea Limited</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it expected tea production for the year to October 31, 1997 to exceed 8,000 tonnes, to around last year's output of 8,909 tonnes. It forecast coffee output at over 600 tonnes compared to 386 tonnes grown during the period under review. It also anticipated a strong growth trend, particularly in its export sales, on the back of better yields and quality of both crops in the current year.</p>
<p>----Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9----</p>
</text>
